FastAPI is a modern high performance web framework for building APIs with framework.

FastAPI is built on famous libraries of python : 1. Starlette  2. Pydantic

Starlette manages how your API receives request and sends back responses.(receives and sends request)

pydantic is used to check if the API is correct and in the right format.(corret format)

earlier system that were used to build api has issue of performance 

philosophy of API :(why called fast API)
1. Fast to run 
2. Fast to code (less number of lines)

Q. how fast api run : (why prefer fast API over flask)
client sends a http request to webserver which is first received by SGI then SGI converts it to python understandable code (api code) 
webserver(http code) ----> SGI(converts http code to python understadable code and vise versa)-----> API code 
SGI:(Server gateway interface) communicator between web server and API code
SGI is of two types: 
1. WSGI "Webserver gateway interface"(used in flask can process single request at a time"Synchronuous in nature" bloking in nature like at a time when 1 process is transalating other one waits" Werkzeug WSGI library)
webserver(Gunicorn) ----> WSGI(wekzeug) -----> API code(Synchronous endpoint)
2. ASGI(used in fastapi)"Asynchronous gateway interface"
webserver(uvicorn) ------> ASGI(starlette) ------> API code (ASynchronous endpoint supports async and await function of python used for parallel processing)

Q. why fast api are fast to code?
1. Automatic input validation(using pydantic)
2. Auto generated Interactive Documentation
3. Seamless Integration with modern Ecosystem(Ml/DL libraries,OAuth,JWT,SQL Alchemy,Docker,Kubernetes etc)

