HTTP Status codes:
these are 3 digit number returned by a web server(like FastAPI) to indicate the result of a clients request(like browser or API consumer)
they help the client (browser,frontned,mabile):
-- whether the request was successful
-- whether something went wrong
-- and what kind of issue occured
2xx  --> success
3xx --> redirection
4xx --> client error
5xx --> server error

200 -> standard success  -> get or post succeded
201 created -> resource created  -> after post
204 no content -> success but ot data returned  -> delete 
400 bad request -> malformed or invalid request -> missing field wrong data type
401 unauthorised -> no/ invalid authentication -> login required
403 forbidden -> authenticated, but not permission -> logged in but not allowed
404 not found -> resource dosen't exists -> patient_id not in DB
500 internal server error -> generic faliure -> something broke on server
502 bad gateway -> gateway(like Ngnix) failed to reach backend
503 service unavailable -> server is down or overloaded  

HTTP Extension :
it is a special built-in exception in fast API used to return custom HTTP error responses when something goes wrong in your API 
Instead of returning a normal JSON or crashing the server, you can generally raise an error with:
1. a proper HTTP status code
2. a custom error msg
3. (optional) extra headers


Query Parameter : (view patets data in a sorted manner on nay criteria in asc or dsc)
query - parameter are optional key_value pairs appended to the end of a url used to pass aditional data to the server in an HTTP request. They are typically employed for operations like filtering, sorting,searching and pagination without altering the endpoint path itself.

example : /patients?city=Delhi&sort_by=age
> the ? marks the start of query parameters
> each parameter is a key value - pair pair
> multiple parameters are separated by & 

query() is a utility function provided by fastAPI to declare, validate and document query parameters in your API endpoints.

it allows you to :
- set default value
- enforce validation rules
- add metadata like description

